aising or campaign infrastructure. Balint has raised over $950,000 and holds more than $600,000 on hand, while Malloy has under $20,000 available and no outside spending on either side.\n\nRecent polling is consistent: UNH surveys show Balint leading by 30 or more points among likely voters, and a September Braun Research poll shows a smaller but still commanding advantage. Prediction markets give Balint roughly a 98% chance of winning, and the Cook Political Report called the race a cruise for the incumbent. The fundamentals, money, and polling all align on a comfortable Democratic win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9976, "margin": 26.51}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9992, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9998, "margin": 33.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 32.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9977, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9974, "margin": 25.0}]}